  "scientific_question": "Do donors with more CA1 pyramidal neurons embedded in reactive-astrocyte niches that also contain nearby lymphocytes show faster memory decline beyond the current CA1 neuron-loss and reactive-gliosis panel?",
  "approach": "Assign cells to CA1 using annotation polygons after dividing polygon coordinates by 16. From ClassificationNode labels, select CA1 Pyramidal Neuron, Reactive Astrocyte, and Lymphocyte centroids. For each CA1 pyramidal neuron, test whether at least one CA1 reactive astrocyte lies within radius R and at least one CA1 lymphocyte lies within the same radius R. The donor-level biomarker is the fraction of CA1 pyramidal neurons satisfying both conditions. If there are no CA1 pyramidal neurons, return NaN; otherwise return 0 when no qualifying niche is present.",
